{"id": "unknown-2026-10-09-021", "date": "2026-10-09", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q4", "month": 10, "week": 41, "weekday": "Fri"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["food_safety", "industry_general"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Miami company recalls sprouts in Florida, New Hampshire because of E. coli contamination", "content": "<p>LEASA Industries Co. Inc. of Miami, FL, has recalled its alfalfa sprouts because of possible contamination with E. coli.</p><p>The recall was not posted on the Food and Drug Administration&#x2019;s main recall page, but was posted on its <a href=\"https://www.accessdata.fda.gov/scripts/ires/?Event=99951&amp;ref=foodsafetynews.com\"><u>enforcement report</u></a>, which is relatively obscure and not widely available</p>", "sources": [{"name": "food_safety_news", "url": "https://www.foodsafetynews.com/2026/10/miami-company-recalls-sprouts-in-florida-new-hampshire-because-of-e-coli-contamination/", "type": "rss"}]}
